```python
# ============================================================
# CONCEPT 5: COMMON MIGRATION ERRORS AND FIXES
# ============================================================

# ERROR 1: "No changes detected"
python manage.py makemigrations
# Means: Django sees no changes in models.py
# Fix: make sure you saved models.py, app is in INSTALLED_APPS

# ERROR 2: "Table already exists"
# Means: migration ran twice
# Fix: check migration files, delete db.sqlite3 and start fresh if needed

# ERROR 3: "Field does not exist"
# Means: you're accessing field that wasn't in model when migration ran
# Fix: add field to model, run makemigrations + migrate again

# ADDING NEW FIELD TO EXISTING MODEL:
class Post(models.Model):
    title = models.CharField(max_length=200)
    content = models.TextField()
    created_at = models.DateTimeField(auto_now_add=True)
    is_published = models.BooleanField(default=False)
    views_count = models.IntegerField(default=0)
    # added new field — must run makemigrations + migrate again
    # default=0 required for existing rows that don't have this field yet

# Run:
# python manage.py makemigrations   ← creates new migration file (0002_...)
# python manage.py migrate          ← adds column to existing table
```

